## 2-minute demo script

- 0:00-0:15 Problem: students use AI anyway, unguarded AI hurts exam performance, professors fly blind until the midterm. The university's answer is not a ban, it is "if you use AI, use Margin".
- 0:15-1:00 Student view: ask "just give me the code", get a nudge, escalate to a slide reference, try the jailbreak and watch the guard catch it (debug drawer visible). Photo red-circle if reliable, otherwise typed work.
- 1:00-1:45 Professor view: heatmap, one student's three-line summary, the "reteach base cases Thursday" card.
- 1:45-2:00 Close: Harvard's CS50 already says if you use AI, use ours. Margin brings that to every course.
- Rehearse the demo path until it works 5 times in a row. Run real sessions beforehand so the dashboard has something to show. Do not fill it with invented rows.

